    {
      "annotation_id": "e7fdcc6d157c402c8e09d1ef118eb64b_77",
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "labels": [
        "ISSUE"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:issue"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "14. In view of above, question for consideration before this court is whether after repeal of earlier Act and introduction of new Act which contains the lesser punishment, the court can take a lenient view of awarding the lesser punishment."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a8df91795839434789f746c30142423f_78",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On this issue, Hon'ble Supreme Court in case titled as M/s A. K. Sarkar & Company & Anr. Vs. The State of Digitally signed by Kiran Kiran Gupta Date:\n Gupta 2024.07.03  15:16:55  +0530 West Bengal & Ors, Special Leave Petition(Criminal) No."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1395830d58094a0ab8263c859fcb1fb4_79",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This court in T. Barai VS. Henry Ah Hoe (1983) 1 SCC 177, had held that when an amendment is beneficial to the accused it can be applied even to cases pending the courts where such a provision did not exist at the time of commission of offe"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "abe2669f1d244f78a25883fdec104832_80",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "15. The recent judgment of Hon'ble Supreme Court in case M/s A. K. Sarkar & Company & Anr.\n(Supra) has made it clear that if there is an amendment in the Act, which is beneficial to the accused,\nit can be applied even to the pending cases i"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "dc9c1efcabd54546945d554e70c7ed44_81",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe ratio of judgment M/s A. K. Sarkar & Company & Anr. (Supra) is squarely applicable to the facts of present case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "488ab97dae9b43fb93e0f650f259fa21_82",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore on the basis of above case law, I have no hesitation to hold that this court can take a lenient view as per new provisions of law."
    },
